Exception) before delegating.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'strategy', 'value': 'validStrategyMock'}, {'parameter': 'startIndex', 'value': '1000'}, {'parameter': 'finishIndex', 'value': '1010'}], 'expected': 'IndexOutOfBoundsException', 'description': 'Start index exceeds the size of the underlying BarSeries. The method should detect the out‑of‑range index and throw an IndexOutOfBoundsException.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'strategy', 'value': 'validStrategyMock'}, {'parameter': 'startIndex', 'value': '0'}, {'parameter': 'finishIndex', 'value': '1000'}], 'expected': 'IndexOutOfBoundsException', 'description': 'Finish index exceeds the size of the BarSeries. The method should validate the upper bound and throw an IndexOutOfBoundsException.'}]}, {'group': 'BarSeriesManager.run(Strategy,int,int) - additional scenarios', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'strategy', 'value': 'validStrategyMock'}, {'parameter': 'startIndex', 'value': '2'}, {'parameter': 'finishIndex', 'value': '-1'}], 'expected': 'IllegalArgumentException', 'description': 'Negative finishIndex should be rejected. The method must validate that both indexes are non‑negative and throw IllegalArgumentException before any processing.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'strategy', 'value': 'validStrategyMock'}, {'parameter': 'startIndex', 'value': '0'}, {'parameter': 'finishIndex', 'value': '0'}], 'expected': 'non‑null TradingRecord instance with zero trades (empty record)', 'description': 'Run on an empty BarSeries (size 0). With startIndex == finishIndex == 0 the manager should return an empty TradingRecord without throwing an exception.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'strategy', 'value': 'validStrategyMock'}, {'parameter': 'startIndex', 'value': '0'}, {'parameter': 'finishIndex', 'value': '9'}], 'expected': 'non‑null TradingRecord instance containing the trades generated by the strategy over the whole series', 'description': 'Boundary test where the range covers the entire BarSeries (size 10, indexes 0‑9). The method